post_content:
A $12 beer-and-a-shot combo on the Strip, inside a hotel that could easily charge double — that alone is worth knowing about at this New York-New York bar.

<strong>Order This:</strong>

Grab the beer and a shot combo for $12, or keep it simple with a $7 draft beer. House wine and well cocktails run $8 each — not dirt cheap, but fair for a spot sitting dead center on Las Vegas Boulevard.

This is a Strip bar that doesn't need gimmicks to earn a stop — it's got 14 flat-screen TVs for catching every game, plus bar-top gaming if you'd rather play a hand between rounds. The dueling pianos show that made this place famous doesn't kick off until 8 PM, so happy hour is actually the quiet window — good drinks, good prices, none of the noise. Get in, get comfortable, and beat the crowd that shows up later for the show.

Happy hour runs daily from 4-7 PM. Located inside New York-New York at 3790 S Las Vegas Blvd.

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;
<h4></h4>
&nbsp;

&nbsp;

*Note: This listing has not been verified. No Happy Hour menu or prices on their website. Call ahead before making the trip. 1 702-463-2700
<h2 style="text-align: center;">Nene Japanese Contemporary Bistro Happy Hour</h2>
Enjoy Happy Hour at Nene Japanese Contemporary Bistro with expertly crafted cocktails, sake specials, and fresh Japanese-inspired bites in a sleek, modern setting. It’s a refined spot to unwind and savor bold, elevated flavors.

&nbsp;

&nbsp;
<h3></h3>

DRNK at Durango Casino offers a lively, upscale setting to sip and socialize with expertly crafted cocktails, beer, and wine at great prices. With its sleek bar atmosphere and inviting vibe, it’s the perfect place to unwind, meet friends, and enjoy a stylish start to your evening.

DRNK doesn't offer a formal happy hour. Instead they serve $3 shots, $3 beer and $1.99 Cuervo Margaritas all day.

&nbsp;

